# Experiment report: FrozenLake-v1 (4x4, slippery)

## Method
Tabular Q-learning (Sutton & Barto, section 6.5): off-policy TD control with an
epsilon-greedy behaviour policy and a greedy target. The final policy is
greedy with respect to the learned Q-table (`policy.py`), stored as data
(`q.npy`, 16x4).

## Hyperparameters
| Name | Value |
|---|---|
| episodes | 30000 |
| gamma | 0.99 |
| alpha | linear 0.2 → 0.01 |
| epsilon | linear 1.0 → 0.05 over the first 60 % of episodes |
| tie-breaking | random among maximal actions |
| seed | 1234 |

## Experiments
| Run | Seed | Extra args | Exit | Train s | Dev episodes | Dev mean return |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| r1 | 1234 | - | 0 | 8.3 | 200 | 0.800 |

## Results
Mean return (success rate) of the greedy policy on 200 dev episodes,
evaluated by the harness: **0.800** (threshold 0.7).

## Limitations
- Slippery dynamics cap the success rate near 0.74 even for the optimal policy;
  differences between runs below about 0.02 are evaluation noise.
- The learning rate schedule was not tuned beyond a handful of runs.
